# API Configuration

## Environment Variables

### Required (Optional for API mode)
- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` - Your OpenRouter API key
- `KILO_API_KEY` - Your Kilo API key
- `GROQ_API_KEY` - Your Groq API key
- `HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY` - Your HuggingFace API key

### Free-Tier Providers
- `GOOGLE_API_KEY` - Your Google Gemini API key (free tier available)
- `MISTRAL_API_KEY` - Your Mistral API key (free tier available)
- `TOGETHER_API_KEY` - Your Together AI API key (free tier available)
- `COHERE_API_KEY` - Your Cohere API key (trial free tier available)

### Paid Providers
- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` - Your Anthropic API key
- `PERPLEXITY_API_KEY` - Your Perplexity API key

### Optional (For scraping fallback)
- `PORT` - Server port (default: 3000)
- `OLLAMA_WEB_URL` - Ollama web UI URL for scraping

## Usage

### With API Keys (Official API mode)
```bash
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY="sk-or-v1-..."
export GOOGLE_API_KEY="..."
bun run src/index.ts
```

### Without API Keys (Scraper fallback mode)
```bash
bun run src/index.ts
```

The server will automatically:
1. Try to use official APIs if credentials exist
2. Fall back to web scraping if no credentials or API fails
3. Prioritize free-tier providers when listing all models
